  <script type="application/json" data-target="react-app.embeddedData">{"payload":{"codeViewBlobRoute":{"csv":null,"csvError":null,"headerInfo":{"toc":[{"level":1,"text":"PackWrite","anchor":"packwrite","htmlText":"PackWrite"},{"level":2,"text":"Contents","anchor":"contents","htmlText":"Contents"},{"level":2,"text":"Why PackWrite","anchor":"why-packwrite","htmlText":"Why PackWrite"},{"level":2,"text":"Readiness and scope","anchor":"readiness-and-scope","htmlText":"Readiness and scope"},{"level":2,"text":"Install","anchor":"install","htmlText":"Install"},{"level":2,"text":"Quickstart","anchor":"quickstart","htmlText":"Quickstart"},{"level":2,"text":"Commands","anchor":"commands","htmlText":"Commands"},{"level":3,"text":"init options","anchor":"init-options","htmlText":"init options"},{"level":2,"text":"Configuration","anchor":"configuration","htmlText":"Configuration"},{"level":2,"text":"Model / provider selection","anchor":"model--provider-selection","htmlText":"Model / provider selection"},{"level":2,"text":"Model response format","anchor":"model-response-format","htmlText":"Model response format"},{"level":2,"text":"Generated /agent structure","anchor":"generated-agent-structure","htmlText":"Generated /agent structure"},{"level":2,"text":"Security \u0026 privacy","anchor":"security--privacy","htmlText":"Security \u0026amp; privacy"},{"level":2,"text":"Workflows","anchor":"workflows","htmlText":"Workflows"},{"level":2,"text":"Output \u0026 exit codes","anchor":"output--exit-codes","htmlText":"Output \u0026amp; exit codes"},{"level":2,"text":"Documentation","anchor":"documentation","htmlText":"Documentation"},{"level":2,"text":"Development","anchor":"development","htmlText":"Development"},{"level":2,"text":"Project status","anchor":"project-status","htmlText":"Project status"},{"level":2,"text":"Contributing, security, license","anchor":"contributing-security-license","htmlText":"Contributing, security, license"},{"level":2,"text":"About Kujo","anchor":"about-kujo","htmlText":"About Kujo"}]},"issueTemplate":null,"discussionTemplate":null,"richText":"\u003carticle class=\"markdown-body entry-content container-lg\" itemprop=\"text\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003ePackWrite\u003c/h1\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-packwrite\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: PackWrite\" href=\"#packwrite\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/kujolang/packwrite/releases/tag/v1.1.1\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/03438ac5d105d8c0163024798193b72e542e9635a1ec8d268fcaac5c601b61c8/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f76657273696f6e2d312e312e312d626c61636b\" alt=\"Version\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/version-1.1.1-black\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/LICENSE\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/be07a68b57a673af622198c336264f89d82bf4cd5d87bc0cb3f7b6ae47cc43ea/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f6c6963656e73652d4d49542d6c6967687467726579\" alt=\"License\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-lightgrey\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/kujolang/kujo\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/6b3480f7d340221eb016f867281fb8ec9c90042bc68ea9e663eb4651d2bb75f1/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f6275696c74253230776974682d4b756a6f2d77686974652e737667\" alt=\"built with Kujo\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/built%20with-Kujo-white.svg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePackWrite turns a project brief into a validated execution pack for coding agents.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eSave your brief as \u003ccode\u003eMEGA_PROMPT.md\u003c/code\u003e and run PackWrite in your repository. It sends\nthe brief and a small repository summary to a model, then writes an \u003ccode\u003eagent/\u003c/code\u003e directory\nwith phase plans, acceptance criteria, handoff notes, and review prompts. PackWrite\nchecks the pack's structure and paths; you review its content before using it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"strategy AI → MEGA_PROMPT.md → packwrite → /agent pack → implementation agent → reviewer\"\u003e\u003cpre lang=\"text\" class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003estrategy AI → MEGA_PROMPT.md → packwrite → /agent pack → implementation agent → reviewer\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eContents\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-contents\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Contents\" href=\"#contents\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#why-packwrite\"\u003eWhy PackWrite\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#readiness-and-scope\"\u003eReadiness and scope\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#install\"\u003eInstall\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#quickstart\"\u003eQuickstart\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#commands\"\u003eCommands\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#configuration\"\u003eConfiguration\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#model--provider-selection\"\u003eModel / provider selection\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#model-response-format\"\u003eModel response format\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#generated-agent-structure\"\u003eGenerated \u003ccode\u003e/agent\u003c/code\u003e structure\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#security--privacy\"\u003eSecurity \u0026amp; privacy\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#workflows\"\u003eWorkflows\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#output--exit-codes\"\u003eOutput \u0026amp; exit codes\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#documentation\"\u003eDocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#development\"\u003eDevelopment\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#project-status\"\u003eProject status\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"#contributing-security-license\"\u003eContributing, security, license\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhy PackWrite\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-why-packwrite\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Why PackWrite\" href=\"#why-packwrite\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eA large task needs a record of its scope, progress, and decisions. PackWrite keeps\nthat record beside your code:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003eMASTER.md\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e — stable project intent + assumptions (don't rewrite).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003ephases/*.md\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e — per-phase specs with scope, out-of-scope, and acceptance criteria.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003eHANDOFF.md\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003eDECISIONS.md\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e — mutable state and a decision log.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003eREVIEW_CHECKLIST.md\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e — concrete, verifiable review items.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003eDEEPSEEK_START.md\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003eCODEX_REVIEW_PROMPT.md\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e — ready-to-paste prompts for an\nimplementation agent and an independent reviewer.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eCode validates the required files, sections, and paths. The model writes the content.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eReadiness and scope\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-readiness-and-scope\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Readiness and scope\" href=\"#readiness-and-scope\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003ePackWrite creates local planning files. It does not implement your project, deploy\ncode, or coordinate concurrent writers. Review generated instructions before giving\nthem to an agent. Hosted authentication, organization policy, signing, and deployment\ncontrols belong to the systems that run PackWrite.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eCurrent hardening includes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOutput directories must be relative, non-empty, non-traversing paths.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eModel manifest paths are validated before dry-runs or writes claim success.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSecret-looking generated paths are rejected, not merely warned about after writing.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWrites are staged and validated before promotion, with rollback on failed promotion.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe full test suite is offline: 248 unit assertions and 116 CLI integration assertions.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eInstall\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-install\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Install\" href=\"#install\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003ePackWrite is written in the \u003ca href=\"#about-kujo\"\u003eKujo language\u003c/a\u003e and run by the Kujo\ninterpreter. Install Kujo so the \u003ccode\u003ekujo\u003c/code\u003e command is available on your \u003ccode\u003ePATH\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"# get the released source\ngit clone --branch v1.1.1 --depth 1 https://github.com/kujolang/packwrite.git\ncd packwrite\n./bin/packwrite --help\n\n# or install the launcher on your PATH\nmake install                      # symlinks bin/packwrite into /usr/local/bin\npackwrite --help\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e get the released source\u003c/span\u003e\ngit clone --branch v1.1.1 --depth 1 https://github.com/kujolang/packwrite.git\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e packwrite\n./bin/packwrite --help\n\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e or install the launcher on your PATH\u003c/span\u003e\nmake install                      \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e symlinks bin/packwrite into /usr/local/bin\u003c/span\u003e\npackwrite --help\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe destination \u003ccode\u003ePREFIX/bin\u003c/code\u003e must already exist and be writable. Set \u003ccode\u003ePREFIX\u003c/code\u003e to\nchoose a different install root, for example \u003ccode\u003emake install PREFIX=\"$HOME/.local\"\u003c/code\u003e.\nInstallation returns a nonzero status if the symlink cannot be created.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe launcher preserves your working directory, so config discovery and the generated\n\u003ccode\u003e/agent\u003c/code\u003e pack land where you invoke it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eQuickstart\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-quickstart\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Quickstart\" href=\"#quickstart\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"cd my-project\ncat \u0026gt; MEGA_PROMPT.md \u0026lt;\u0026lt;'EOF'\n# Demo\n\nBuild a small CLI that says hello, with tests and a README.\nEOF\n\nexport PACKWRITE_API_KEY=sk-...                       # your provider key (env only)\npackwrite doctor\npackwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --dry-run\npackwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --provider deepseek --model deepseek-v4-pro\npackwrite validate\npackwrite prompt deepseek         # paste into your implementation agent\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e my-project\ncat \u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e MEGA_PROMPT.md \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003e\u0026lt;\u0026lt;\u003c/span\u003e'\u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003eEOF\u003c/span\u003e'\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e# Demo\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003eBuild a small CLI that says hello, with tests and a README.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003eEOF\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-k\"\u003eexport\u003c/span\u003e PACKWRITE_API_KEY=sk-...                       \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e your provider key (env only)\u003c/span\u003e\npackwrite doctor\npackwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --dry-run\npackwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --provider deepseek --model deepseek-v4-pro\npackwrite validate\npackwrite prompt deepseek         \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e paste into your implementation agent\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eA successful \u003ccode\u003einit\u003c/code\u003e prints:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"PackWrite generated an agent pack.\n\n  Output:     agent/\n  Provider:   deepseek\n  Model:      deepseek-v4-pro\n  Files:      13\n  Phases:     6\n  Validation: passed with 0 warnings\n\nNext:\n  packwrite prompt deepseek\"\u003e\u003cpre lang=\"text\" class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003ePackWrite generated an agent pack.\n\n  Output:     agent/\n  Provider:   deepseek\n  Model:      deepseek-v4-pro\n  Files:      13\n  Phases:     6\n  Validation: passed with 0 warnings\n\nNext:\n  packwrite prompt deepseek\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003einit\u003c/code\u003e prints each stage, such as \u003ccode\u003e[3/8] Collecting repository context...\u003c/code\u003e.\nUse \u003ccode\u003e--quiet\u003c/code\u003e to suppress successful progress and summary output.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e--dry-run\u003c/code\u003e calls the model and validates the returned manifest without writing a\npack. It can incur provider charges:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"packwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --dry-run\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003epackwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --dry-run\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eNew here? Follow the full walkthrough in \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/HOWTO.md\"\u003edocs/HOWTO.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eCommands\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-commands\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Commands\" href=\"#commands\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eCommand\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eWhat it does\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003epackwrite init [file]\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eGenerate an \u003ccode\u003e/agent\u003c/code\u003e pack from a mega prompt\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003epackwrite validate\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eDeterministically validate an existing \u003ccode\u003e/agent\u003c/code\u003e pack (\u003ccode\u003e--json\u003c/code\u003e for CI)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003epackwrite summary\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eReport pack status, phase count, missing files, warnings, and next command (\u003ccode\u003e--json\u003c/code\u003e supported)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003epackwrite prompt deepseek\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ePrint the implementation-agent prompt\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003epackwrite prompt codex-review\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ePrint the reviewer prompt\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003epackwrite config\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eShow the fully resolved configuration and its sources\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003epackwrite doctor\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eCheck config, provider, endpoint, API key, and prompt/output state (\u003ccode\u003e--strict\u003c/code\u003e gates CI; \u003ccode\u003e--json\u003c/code\u003e is machine-readable)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003epackwrite help\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003eversion\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eHelp / version\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003ePackWrite supports top-level help/version aliases and command-specific \u003ccode\u003e--help\u003c/code\u003e for\n\u003ccode\u003einit\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003evalidate\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003esummary\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eprompt\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003econfig\u003c/code\u003e, and \u003ccode\u003edoctor\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch3 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003einit\u003c/code\u003e options\u003c/h3\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-init-options\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: init options\" href=\"#init-options\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"--provider \u0026lt;name\u0026gt;     deepseek | openai | local (OpenAI-compatible; others need --endpoint)\n--model \u0026lt;name\u0026gt;        model identifier\n--endpoint \u0026lt;url\u0026gt;      OpenAI-compatible chat-completions URL (overrides the preset)\n--temperature \u0026lt;n\u0026gt;     sampling temperature (0.0–2.0)\n--timeout \u0026lt;seconds\u0026gt;   request timeout (positive number)\n--output \u0026lt;dir\u0026gt;        output pack directory (default: agent)\n--overwrite           replace an existing pack directory (clean replace: stale files pruned)\n--dry-run             parse + plan but write nothing\n--config \u0026lt;file\u0026gt;       use a specific packwrite.toml\n--verbose             extra diagnostics\n--quiet               suppress successful progress and summary output\n--debug               print sanitized provider/model/finish_reason diagnostics\n--save-raw-response \u0026lt;file\u0026gt;  save raw model response (may contain sensitive data)\"\u003e\u003cpre lang=\"text\" class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003e--provider \u0026lt;name\u0026gt;     deepseek | openai | local (OpenAI-compatible; others need --endpoint)\n--model \u0026lt;name\u0026gt;        model identifier\n--endpoint \u0026lt;url\u0026gt;      OpenAI-compatible chat-completions URL (overrides the preset)\n--temperature \u0026lt;n\u0026gt;     sampling temperature (0.0–2.0)\n--timeout \u0026lt;seconds\u0026gt;   request timeout (positive number)\n--output \u0026lt;dir\u0026gt;        output pack directory (default: agent)\n--overwrite           replace an existing pack directory (clean replace: stale files pruned)\n--dry-run             parse + plan but write nothing\n--config \u0026lt;file\u0026gt;       use a specific packwrite.toml\n--verbose             extra diagnostics\n--quiet               suppress successful progress and summary output\n--debug               print sanitized provider/model/finish_reason diagnostics\n--save-raw-response \u0026lt;file\u0026gt;  save raw model response (may contain sensitive data)\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eConfiguration\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-configuration\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Configuration\" href=\"#configuration\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003ePackWrite reads \u003ccode\u003epackwrite.toml\u003c/code\u003e from the working directory. Resolution order, lowest to\nhighest precedence:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"defaults  \u0026lt;  global config (~/.config/packwrite/config.toml)  \u0026lt;  packwrite.toml  \u0026lt;  CLI flags\"\u003e\u003cpre lang=\"text\" class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003edefaults  \u0026lt;  global config (~/.config/packwrite/config.toml)  \u0026lt;  packwrite.toml  \u0026lt;  CLI flags\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-toml notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"[prompt]\nfile = \u0026quot;MEGA_PROMPT.md\u0026quot;\n\n[output]\ndir = \u0026quot;agent\u0026quot;\noverwrite = false\nmode = \u0026quot;autopilot\u0026quot;          # reserved (parsed, not yet wired)\n\n[model]\nprovider = \u0026quot;deepseek\u0026quot;\nmodel = \u0026quot;deepseek-v4-pro\u0026quot;\ntemperature = 0.1\n# endpoint = \u0026quot;https://api.deepseek.com/chat/completions\u0026quot;   # override the preset\n\n[repo_context]\n# include = top-level allow-list; omit for defaults, use [] for all eligible names\ninclude = [\u0026quot;README.md\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;Cargo.toml\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;package.json\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;pyproject.toml\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;src\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;tests\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;docs\u0026quot;]\nexclude = [\u0026quot;.env\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;.git\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;node_modules\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;vendor\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;dist\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;build\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;.next\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;coverage\u0026quot;]\n\n[pack]\nmin_phases = 6              # validation warns below this\nmax_phases = 12             # included in the model instructions\ninclude_deepseek_prompt = true        # generate + require DEEPSEEK_START.md\ninclude_codex_review_prompt = true    # generate + require CODEX_REVIEW_PROMPT.md\ninclude_review_checklist = true       # generate + require REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003e[\u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003eprompt\u003c/span\u003e]\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003efile\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003eMEGA_PROMPT.md\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n\n[\u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003eoutput\u003c/span\u003e]\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003edir\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003eagent\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003eoverwrite\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003efalse\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003emode\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003eautopilot\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e reserved (parsed, not yet wired)\u003c/span\u003e\n\n[\u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003emodel\u003c/span\u003e]\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003eprovider\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003edeepseek\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003emodel\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003edeepseek-v4-pro\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003etemperature\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e0.1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e endpoint = \"https://api.deepseek.com/chat/completions\"   # override the preset\u003c/span\u003e\n\n[\u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003erepo_context\u003c/span\u003e]\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e include = top-level allow-list; omit for defaults, use [] for all eligible names\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003einclude\u003c/span\u003e = [\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003eREADME.md\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003eCargo.toml\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003epackage.json\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003epyproject.toml\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003esrc\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003etests\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003edocs\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e]\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003eexclude\u003c/span\u003e = [\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e.env\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e.git\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003enode_modules\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003evendor\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003edist\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003ebuild\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e.next\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003ecoverage\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e]\n\n[\u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003epack\u003c/span\u003e]\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003emin_phases\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e6\u003c/span\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e validation warns below this\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003emax_phases\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e12\u003c/span\u003e             \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e included in the model instructions\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003einclude_deepseek_prompt\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e generate + require DEEPSEEK_START.md\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003einclude_codex_review_prompt\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e generate + require CODEX_REVIEW_PROMPT.md\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003cspan class=\"pl-smi\"\u003einclude_review_checklist\u003c/span\u003e = \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e       \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e generate + require REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eAll keys above change observable behavior \u003cstrong\u003eexcept\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003e[output].mode\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003erun_name\u003c/code\u003e\n(via \u003ccode\u003e--run-name\u003c/code\u003e), which are parsed but \u003cstrong\u003ereserved\u003c/strong\u003e for deferred features. Full table\nwith types, defaults, and flag mappings: \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/CONFIGURATION.md\"\u003edocs/CONFIGURATION.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e.\nSee also \u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/packwrite.example.toml\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003epackwrite.example.toml\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eModel / provider selection\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-model--provider-selection\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Model / provider selection\" href=\"#model--provider-selection\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eChoose a provider and model with flags or config. PackWrite calls the Kujo\n\u003ccode\u003eai_chat\u003c/code\u003e builtin through an adapter.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe adapter speaks only the OpenAI-compatible chat-completions protocol\u003c/strong\u003e (it posts\n\u003ccode\u003e{model, messages}\u003c/code\u003e, authenticates with \u003ccode\u003eAuthorization: Bearer\u003c/code\u003e, and reads\n\u003ccode\u003echoices[0].message.content\u003c/code\u003e). Built-in endpoint presets therefore exist only for\nproviders that expose that protocol natively:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003e\u003ccode\u003e--provider\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eEndpoint preset\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003edeepseek\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehttps://api.deepseek.com/chat/completions\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eopenai\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehttps://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003elocal\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehttp://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eAny other provider has \u003cstrong\u003eno preset\u003c/strong\u003e and must point \u003ccode\u003e--endpoint\u003c/code\u003e (or \u003ccode\u003e[model].endpoint\u003c/code\u003e)\nat an OpenAI-compatible URL — a gateway such as OpenRouter or LiteLLM works well.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eSet \u003ccode\u003e--model\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003e[model].model\u003c/code\u003e to a model your endpoint supports. The default is\n\u003ccode\u003edeepseek-v4-pro\u003c/code\u003e; check your provider's available models before running generation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAnthropic is not supported natively.\u003c/strong\u003e Anthropic's API uses \u003ccode\u003e/v1/messages\u003c/code\u003e +\n\u003ccode\u003ex-api-key\u003c/code\u003e, which this adapter does not speak. \u003ccode\u003e--provider anthropic\u003c/code\u003e with no endpoint\nfails with a clear error; to use Claude, set \u003ccode\u003e--endpoint\u003c/code\u003e to an OpenAI-compatible\ngateway in front of it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAPI keys come from the environment only\u003c/strong\u003e — never from flags or committed config.\nPackWrite checks \u003ccode\u003ePACKWRITE_API_KEY\u003c/code\u003e first, then a provider-specific variable\n(\u003ccode\u003eDEEPSEEK_API_KEY\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eOPENAI_API_KEY\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eANTHROPIC_API_KEY\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eModel response format\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-model-response-format\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Model response format\" href=\"#model-response-format\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003ePackWrite expects the model to return a \u003cstrong\u003eJSON file manifest\u003c/strong\u003e and nothing else:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"{ \u0026quot;files\u0026quot;: [ { \u0026quot;path\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;agent/MASTER.md\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;content\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;...\u0026quot; }, ... ] }\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003e{ \u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003e\"files\"\u003c/span\u003e: [ { \u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003e\"path\"\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003eagent/MASTER.md\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003e\"content\"\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e...\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e }, \u003cspan class=\"pl-ii\"\u003e... \u003c/span\u003e] }\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eFor DeepSeek structured pack generation, PackWrite requests strict JSON mode and\ndisables thinking by default:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"{\n  \u0026quot;response_format\u0026quot;: { \u0026quot;type\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;json_object\u0026quot; },\n  \u0026quot;thinking\u0026quot;: { \u0026quot;type\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;disabled\u0026quot; },\n  \u0026quot;max_tokens\u0026quot;: 32000,\n  \u0026quot;temperature\u0026quot;: 0.1\n}\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003e{\n  \u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003e\"response_format\"\u003c/span\u003e: { \u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003e\"type\"\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003ejson_object\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e },\n  \u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003e\"thinking\"\u003c/span\u003e: { \u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003e\"type\"\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003edisabled\u003cspan class=\"pl-pds\"\u003e\"\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e },\n  \u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003e\"max_tokens\"\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e32000\u003c/span\u003e,\n  \u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003e\"temperature\"\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003e0.1\u003c/span\u003e\n}\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eParsing is tolerant — surrounding prose and \u003ccode\u003e```\u003c/code\u003e code fences are stripped — but\nthe payload must be valid JSON with a non-empty \u003ccode\u003efiles\u003c/code\u003e array of \u003ccode\u003e{path, content}\u003c/code\u003e\nstring pairs whose paths stay inside the output directory. If the model returns prose\nwithout a JSON object, you get \u003ccode\u003eThe model response could not be parsed into files.\u003c/code\u003e with\nsanitized diagnostics (provider/model/response length/head/tail/finish-reason hints)\nto make failures actionable. There is no Markdown-fallback parser in v1.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eGenerated \u003ccode\u003e/agent\u003c/code\u003e structure\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-generated-agent-structure\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Generated /agent structure\" href=\"#generated-agent-structure\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"agent/\n  MASTER.md               stable project intent + assumptions (don't rewrite)\n  TODO.md                 phase checklist linking each phase file\n  HANDOFF.md              mutable status, updated after every phase\n  DECISIONS.md            confirmed / open / log\n  REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md     concrete, verifiable review items\n  DEEPSEEK_START.md       implementation-agent prompt\n  CODEX_REVIEW_PROMPT.md  reviewer prompt\n  phases/\n    00-project-brief.md\n    01-\u0026lt;slug\u0026gt;.md ... NN-\u0026lt;slug\u0026gt;.md\"\u003e\u003cpre lang=\"text\" class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003eagent/\n  MASTER.md               stable project intent + assumptions (don't rewrite)\n  TODO.md                 phase checklist linking each phase file\n  HANDOFF.md              mutable status, updated after every phase\n  DECISIONS.md            confirmed / open / log\n  REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md     concrete, verifiable review items\n  DEEPSEEK_START.md       implementation-agent prompt\n  CODEX_REVIEW_PROMPT.md  reviewer prompt\n  phases/\n    00-project-brief.md\n    01-\u0026lt;slug\u0026gt;.md ... NN-\u0026lt;slug\u0026gt;.md\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eSecurity \u0026amp; privacy\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-security--privacy\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Security \u0026amp; privacy\" href=\"#security--privacy\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003ePackWrite is conservative about what leaves your machine:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAPI keys are read from the environment only\u003c/strong\u003e — never from flags, config, or logs.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe model receives your mega prompt and a bounded repository summary:\u003c/strong\u003e the root\nname, a one-line README excerpt, detected languages, and included file/directory\nnames. PackWrite does not upload the full checkout. Keep sensitive data out of the\nprompt and README excerpt.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSecrets are excluded by default\u003c/strong\u003e (\u003ccode\u003e.env*\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e*.pem\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e*.key\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eid_rsa\u003c/code\u003e,\n\u003ccode\u003eid_ed25519\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e.git\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003enode_modules\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003evendor\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003edist\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003ebuild\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e.next\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003ecoverage\u003c/code\u003e,\n\u003ccode\u003etarget\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e.venv\u003c/code\u003e, and names containing \u003ccode\u003esecret\u003c/code\u003e/\u003ccode\u003etoken\u003c/code\u003e); skipped paths are reported.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGenerated paths are restricted\u003c/strong\u003e to the output directory (absolute, \u003ccode\u003e..\u003c/code\u003e traversal,\nbackslash-separator, \u003ccode\u003e~\u003c/code\u003e home-expansion, control-character, ambiguous-segment, and\nescaping paths are rejected), configured output directories must be relative project\npaths with no existing symlink components, and generated secret-looking paths are\nrejected. Model responses and generated content have explicit resource ceilings.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePrompt payloads are never logged.\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003e--verbose\u003c/code\u003e reports size only. Explicit raw\nresponse saves are owner-only, atomic, and refuse to overwrite an existing path.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMalformed CLI input fails cleanly\u003c/strong\u003e — bad or out-of-range \u003ccode\u003e--temperature\u003c/code\u003e /\n\u003ccode\u003e--timeout\u003c/code\u003e values return an actionable error instead of crashing the runtime.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eDetails and reporting: \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/SECURITY.md\"\u003eSECURITY.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eWorkflows\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-workflows\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Workflows\" href=\"#workflows\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAutonomous implementation.\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003eagent/DEEPSEEK_START.md\u003c/code\u003e tells the implementation agent\nto run on autopilot: read the pack → implement the first incomplete phase → update\n\u003ccode\u003eHANDOFF\u003c/code\u003e/\u003ccode\u003eDECISIONS\u003c/code\u003e/\u003ccode\u003eREVIEW_CHECKLIST\u003c/code\u003e → mark the TODO item → continue to the next\nphase without human approval → repeat until done, stopping only for defined blockers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIndependent review.\u003c/strong\u003e When implementation is finished, hand a reviewer\n\u003ccode\u003eagent/CODEX_REVIEW_PROMPT.md\u003c/code\u003e. It asks for an overall score, category scores, a\ncomparison against the mega prompt, scope drift, bugs, missing tests, security issues,\nand a step-by-step repair checklist.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eOutput \u0026amp; exit codes\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-output--exit-codes\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Output \u0026amp; exit codes\" href=\"#output--exit-codes\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe Kujo runtime has no separate stderr, so \u003cstrong\u003eall output goes to stdout\u003c/strong\u003e, prefixed so\ncategories stay greppable: \u003ccode\u003ewarning (...)\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e! \u003c/code\u003e (validation warnings), \u003ccode\u003enote:\u003c/code\u003e, and\n\u003ccode\u003eerror:\u003c/code\u003e. Exit codes: \u003ccode\u003e0\u003c/code\u003e success, \u003ccode\u003e1\u003c/code\u003e operational failure, \u003ccode\u003e2\u003c/code\u003e usage error.\n\u003ccode\u003epackwrite prompt \u0026lt;target\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e prints the prompt verbatim so it pipes cleanly.\nA missing prompt uses the built-in fallback. Existing unreadable files, directories,\nand symlinks return an operational error instead of emitting a fallback.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eDocumentation\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-documentation\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Documentation\" href=\"#documentation\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eDoc\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eWhat's in it\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/HOWTO.md\"\u003edocs/HOWTO.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eEnd-to-end walkthrough + recipes\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/CONFIGURATION.md\"\u003edocs/CONFIGURATION.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eEvery config key, type, default, and flag\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\"\u003edocs/ARCHITECTURE.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eModule map, data flow, extension points\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md\"\u003edocs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eEvery error message and its fix\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/NEXT_STEPS.md\"\u003edocs/NEXT_STEPS.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eCurrent prioritized backlog for upcoming work\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/PROVIDERS.md\"\u003edocs/PROVIDERS.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eProvider and gateway compatibility matrix\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md\"\u003edocs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eRepeatable official-release gate\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/AGENTS.md\"\u003eAGENTS.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eOrientation for coding agents working on PackWrite\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eCanonical copyable examples live in this README, \u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/HOWTO.md\"\u003edocs/HOWTO.md\u003c/a\u003e, and\n\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/packwrite.example.toml\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003epackwrite.example.toml\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Test fixtures are behavior\ncontracts, not style examples.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eDevelopment\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-development\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Development\" href=\"#development\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"make test       # kujo check on every file + the full offline suite\nmake check      # lint only\nmake help       # list tasks\"\u003e\u003cpre\u003emake \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003etest\u003c/span\u003e       \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e kujo check on every file + the full offline suite\u003c/span\u003e\nmake check      \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e lint only\u003c/span\u003e\nmake \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003ehelp\u003c/span\u003e       \u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e list tasks\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe suite (248 unit + 116 CLI integration assertions) is \u003cstrong\u003efully offline\u003c/strong\u003e — AI calls go\nthrough a fake-injection seam (\u003ccode\u003ePACKWRITE_FAKE_RESPONSE_FILE\u003c/code\u003e), so no API key or network\nis required. The 24 permission assertions skip under root. See \u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/CONTRIBUTING.md\"\u003eCONTRIBUTING.md\u003c/a\u003e for setup and the Kujo runtime\nconventions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eRoot files are intentionally kept for project entrypoints and governance:\n\u003ccode\u003epackwrite.kujo\u003c/code\u003e is the CLI entrypoint, \u003ccode\u003ebin/packwrite\u003c/code\u003e is the launcher, \u003ccode\u003eMakefile\u003c/code\u003e\ndrives developer tasks, \u003ccode\u003ekujo.toml\u003c/code\u003e identifies the Kujo package, and\n\u003ccode\u003epackwrite.example.toml\u003c/code\u003e is the canonical copyable config. Runtime logic lives under\n\u003ccode\u003esrc/\u003c/code\u003e; tests live under \u003ccode\u003etests/\u003c/code\u003e; user/developer docs live under \u003ccode\u003edocs/\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eProject status\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-project-status\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Project status\" href=\"#project-status\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eImplemented in v1:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003einit\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003evalidate\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003esummary\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eprompt\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003econfig\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003edoctor\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003ehelp\u003c/code\u003e,\n\u003ccode\u003eversion\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePlanned / not implemented\u003c/strong\u003e (running them prints a \"planned for a future version\"\nmessage and exits non-zero): \u003ccode\u003ecompare\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003erepair-pack\u003c/code\u003e. Also deferred: a\nMarkdown-delimiter fallback parser (v1 is JSON-manifest only) and streaming output. See\n\u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#extension-points\"\u003edocs/ARCHITECTURE.md\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eContributing, security, license\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-contributing-security-license\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Contributing, security, license\" href=\"#contributing-security-license\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eContributing:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/CONTRIBUTING.md\"\u003eCONTRIBUTING.md\u003c/a\u003e — setup, conventions, Kujo gotchas, PR process.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSecurity:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/SECURITY.md\"\u003eSECURITY.md\u003c/a\u003e — security model and private reporting.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eChangelog:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/CHANGELOG.md\"\u003eCHANGELOG.md\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLicense:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/LICENSE\"\u003eMIT\u003c/a\u003e © 2026 Robert DeVore.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eAbout Kujo\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-about-kujo\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: About Kujo\" href=\"#about-kujo\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003ePackWrite is a standalone tool in the \u003cstrong\u003eKujo\u003c/strong\u003e ecosystem (alongside RunLedger, Howl,\nYard, and others). It is written in the Kujo language and depends only on the Kujo\ninterpreter; it lives in its own repository and does not modify the Kujo language repo.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/article\u003e","richTextTruncated":false,"renderedFileInfo":null,"symbols":{"timed_out":false,"not_analyzed":false,"symbols":[{"name":"PackWrite","fully_qualified_name":"PackWrite","kind":"section_1","ident_start":2,"ident_end":11,"extent_start":0,"extent_end":16730,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":0,"utf16_col":2},"end":{"line_number":0,"utf16_col":11}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":0,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":387,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Contents","fully_qualified_name":"Contents","kind":"section_2","ident_start":860,"ident_end":868,"extent_start":857,"extent_end":1511,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":17,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":17,"utf16_col":11}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":17,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":36,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Why PackWrite","fully_qualified_name":"Why PackWrite","kind":"section_2","ident_start":1514,"ident_end":1527,"extent_start":1511,"extent_end":2177,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":36,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":36,"utf16_col":16}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":36,"utf16_col":0},"end":{