<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Why PackWrite</h2><a id="user-content-why-packwrite" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Why PackWrite" href="#why-packwrite"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">A large task needs a record of its scope, progress, and decisions. PackWrite keeps
that record beside your code:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong><code>MASTER.md</code></strong> — stable project intent + assumptions (don't rewrite).</li>
<li><strong><code>phases/*.md</code></strong> — per-phase specs with scope, out-of-scope, and acceptance criteria.</li>
<li><strong><code>HANDOFF.md</code> / <code>DECISIONS.md</code></strong> — mutable state and a decision log.</li>
<li><strong><code>REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md</code></strong> — concrete, verifiable review items.</li>
<li><strong><code>DEEPSEEK_START.md</code> / <code>CODEX_REVIEW_PROMPT.md</code></strong> — ready-to-paste prompts for an
implementation agent and an independent reviewer.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Code validates the required files, sections, and paths. The model writes the content.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Readiness and scope</h2><a id="user-content-readiness-and-scope" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Readiness and scope" href="#readiness-and-scope"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">PackWrite creates local planning files. It does not implement your project, deploy
code, or coordinate concurrent writers. Review generated instructions before giving
them to an agent. Hosted authentication, organization policy, signing, and deployment
controls belong to the systems that run PackWrite.</p>
<p dir="auto">Current hardening includes:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Output directories must be relative, non-empty, non-traversing paths.</li>
<li>Model manifest paths are validated before dry-runs or writes claim success.</li>
<li>Secret-looking generated paths are rejected, not merely warned about after writing.</li>
<li>Writes are staged and validated before promotion, with rollback on failed promotion.</li>
<li>The full test suite is offline: 248 unit assertions and 116 CLI integration assertions.</li>
</ul>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Install</h2><a id="user-content-install" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Install" href="#install"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">PackWrite is written in the <a href="#about-kujo">Kujo language</a> and run by the Kujo
interpreter. Install Kujo so the <code>kujo</code> command is available on your <code>PATH</code>:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="# get the released source
git clone --branch v1.1.1 --depth 1 https://github.com/kujolang/packwrite.git
cd packwrite
./bin/packwrite --help

# or install the launcher on your PATH
make install                      # symlinks bin/packwrite into /usr/local/bin
packwrite --help"><pre><span class="pl-c"><span class="pl-c">#</span> get the released source</span>
git clone --branch v1.1.1 --depth 1 https://github.com/kujolang/packwrite.git
<span class="pl-c1">cd</span> packwrite
./bin/packwrite --help

<span class="pl-c"><span class="pl-c">#</span> or install the launcher on your PATH</span>
make install                      <span class="pl-c"><span class="pl-c">#</span> symlinks bin/packwrite into /usr/local/bin</span>
packwrite --help</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">The destination <code>PREFIX/bin</code> must already exist and be writable. Set <code>PREFIX</code> to
choose a different install root, for example <code>make install PREFIX="$HOME/.local"</code>.
Installation returns a nonzero status if the symlink cannot be created.</p>
<p dir="auto">The launcher preserves your working directory, so config discovery and the generated
<code>/agent</code> pack land where you invoke it.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Quickstart</h2><a id="user-content-quickstart" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Quickstart" href="#quickstart"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="cd my-project
cat &gt; MEGA_PROMPT.md &lt;&lt;'EOF'
# Demo

Build a small CLI that says hello, with tests and a README.
EOF

export PACKWRITE_API_KEY=sk-...                       # your provider key (env only)
packwrite doctor
packwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --dry-run
packwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --provider deepseek --model deepseek-v4-pro
packwrite validate
packwrite prompt deepseek         # paste into your implementation agent"><pre><span class="pl-c1">cd</span> my-project
cat <span class="pl-k">&gt;</span> MEGA_PROMPT.md <span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-k">&lt;&lt;</span>'<span class="pl-k">EOF</span>'</span>
<span class="pl-s"># Demo</span>
<span class="pl-s"></span>
<span class="pl-s">Build a small CLI that says hello, with tests and a README.</span>
<span class="pl-s"><span class="pl-k">EOF</span></span>

<span class="pl-k">export</span> PACKWRITE_API_KEY=sk-...                       <span class="pl-c"><span class="pl-c">#</span> your provider key (env only)</span>
packwrite doctor
packwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --dry-run
packwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --provider deepseek --model deepseek-v4-pro
packwrite validate
packwrite prompt deepseek         <span class="pl-c"><span class="pl-c">#</span> paste into your implementation agent</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">A successful <code>init</code> prints:</p>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="PackWrite generated an agent pack.

  Output:     agent/
  Provider:   deepseek
  Model:      deepseek-v4-pro
  Files:      13
  Phases:     6
  Validation: passed with 0 warnings

Next:
  packwrite prompt deepseek"><pre lang="text" class="notranslate"><code>PackWrite generated an agent pack.

  Output:     agent/
  Provider:   deepseek
  Model:      deepseek-v4-pro
  Files:      13
  Phases:     6
  Validation: passed with 0 warnings

Next:
  packwrite prompt deepseek
</code></pre></div>
<p dir="auto"><code>init</code> prints each stage, such as <code>[3/8] Collecting repository context...</code>.
Use <code>--quiet</code> to suppress successful progress and summary output.</p>
<p dir="auto"><code>--dry-run</code> calls the model and validates the returned manifest without writing a
pack. It can incur provider charges:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="packwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --dry-run"><pre>packwrite init MEGA_PROMPT.md --dry-run</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">New here? Follow the full walkthrough in <strong><a href="/kujolang/packwrite/blob/b8467535c74263abc59fd3f48028b67d42cd7e68/docs/HOWTO.md">docs/HOWTO.md</a></strong>.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">Commands</h2><a id="user-content-commands" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: Commands" href="#commands"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Command</th>
<th>What it does</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>packwrite init [file]</code></td>
<td>Generate an <code>/agent</code> pack from a mega prompt</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>packwrite validate</code></td>
<td>Deterministically validate an existing <code>/agent</code> pack (<code>--json</code> for CI)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>packwrite summary</code></td>
<td>Report pack status, phase count, missing files, warnings, and next command (<code>--json</code> supported)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>packwrite prompt deepseek</code></td>
<td>Print the implementation-agent prompt</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>packwrite prompt codex-review</code></td>
<td>Print the reviewer prompt</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>packwrite config</code></td>
<td>Show the fully resolved configuration and its sources</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>packwrite doctor</code></td>
<td>Check config, provider, endpoint, API key, and prompt/output state (<code>--strict</code> gates CI; <code>--json</code> is machine-readable)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>packwrite help</code> / <code>version</code></td>
<td>Help / version</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir="auto">PackWrite supports top-level help/version aliases and command-specific <code>--help</code> for
<code>init</code>, <code>validate</code>, <code>summary</code>, <code>prompt</code>, <code>config</code>, and <code>doctor</code>.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto"><code>init</code> options</h3><a id="user-content-init-options" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: init options" href="#init-options"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="--provider &lt;name&gt;     deepseek | openai | local (OpenAI-compatible; others need --endpoint)
--model &lt;name&gt;        model identifier
--endpoint &lt;url&gt;      OpenAI-compatible chat-completions URL (overrides the preset)
--temperature &lt;n&gt;     sampling temperature (0.0–2.0)
--timeout &lt;seconds&gt;   request timeout (positive number)
--output &lt;dir&gt;        output pack directory (default: agent)
--overwrite           replace an existing pack directory (clean replace: stale files pruned)
--dry-run             parse + plan but write nothing
--config &lt;file&gt;       use a specific packwrite.toml
--verbose             extra diagnostics
--quiet               suppress successful progress and summary output
--debug               print sanitized provider/model/finish_reason diagnostics
--save-raw-response &lt;file&gt;  save raw model response (may contain sensitive data)"><pre lang="text" class="notranslate"><code>--provider &lt;name&gt;     deepseek | openai | local (OpenAI-compatible; others need --endpoint)
--model &lt;name&gt;        model identifier
--endpoint &lt;url&gt;      OpenAI-compatible chat-completions URL (overrides the preset)
--temperature &lt;n&gt;     sampling temperature (0.0–2.0)
--timeout &lt;seconds&gt;   request timeout (positive number)
--output &lt;dir&gt;        output pack directory (default: agent)
--overwrite           replace an existing pack directory (clean replace: stale files pruned)
--dry-run             parse + plan but write nothing
--config &lt;file&gt;       use a specific packwrite.toml
--verbose             extra diagnostics
--quiet               suppress successful progress and summary output
--debug               print sanitized provider/model/finish_reason diagnostics
